    ("3.5", "Transportation distances consistent with known AECN routes and evidenced", "Fail", "Evidence linkage is the Fail: each of the three allocated-distance datapoints ('Allocated Distance AECN to Sopor Quebec (truck)', 'Allocated Distance Sopor Quebec to Opelousas (rail)', 'Allocated Distance Opelousas to B6 (truck)') carries only the Ops Notes, and the route maps and the Watco email are linked to the full-distance datapoints only; the allocated distances feed the three embodied components, so their mileage basis is not attached where it is used, and the attachment gate fails on all three. W2 had the reverse gap (maps linked, Ops Notes not). Values: AECN-SOPOR 107.49722 mi from the 173 km map (173 / 1.609344); rail 2,199 mi from the Watco email 'The total milage for this move was 2199.'; Opelousas-Basco 42.9 mi, the longest of three map routes. Allocated rail 5,588.31 mi matches Ops M38 5,588.31288 (2,199 for each FULL railcar plus 2,199 x SHPX215046's W3 share) and Opelousas-Basco 858 mi matches N38 (42.9 x 2 x 10). Three further gaps: (1) Certify's AECN-SOPOR allocated 818.69019 mi does not reproduce from Ops L38 818.7957175 mi (the Ops method with 107.49722 mi gives 818.77454), 0.10553 mi apart, effect 0.000025 t; (2) railcar notes M10 (GPRX5102) and M12 (TILX200231) state 'Mileage (AECN->SOPOR / Rail / Opel->Basco) intentionally left BLANK -- no independently sourced route-mileage reference found for this railcar', yet J/K/L on both rows hold 107.5 / 2199 / 42.9 and feed the allocations, so the attached Ops Notes tells a verifier its own mileage is unsourced; (3) the Watco email names no railcar, route or date, so it cannot tie 2,199 mi to these three moves. [log:certify.attachment_gate, certify.attachment_map, route_evidence.aecn_sopor_map, route_evidence.watco_email, route_evidence.opel_basco_map, ops_notes.rollup, ops_notes.railcars, certify.components, recompute.findings]", "Transport Emissions Acctg v1.1"),
