    ('3.7', 'Billing documents present and consistent with BOL', 'Flag', "Each BOL PDF bundles the Straight BOL, the Shipping Details, the BioEnergie weigh ticket, the TSCA certificate and a Charm PO; all 9 read, and each weigh-ticket net equals the Ops Notes mass. Hygiene: the PO on page 5 of every bundle is Q42025 of 10/2/2025 (line 'Q32025', Ship To El Dorado, KS; see 1.5), and its seller signature is blank on 2462-R, 2463-R, 2464-R, 2468-R, 2469-R and 2470-R; 2457-R ('Correction poids vide et litres finaux') has its 'Tanker Tare wt(empty) (Kg)' hand-corrected 19,282 to 19,290 and litres 21,673 to 21,666 while the printed 25.99 MT was not recomputed (weigh-ticket net 25,980 kg), and Ops M10 describes that correction in 'lb'; 2458-R carries a handwritten 'correction poid vide/empty truck' (page 1 tare 19,130 against page 2 19,460). COBB Loads tab still records 2457-R as 25.99 MT and GPRX5102 as 77.95 MT. [log:bols.per_bol, bols.cross_check, bols.po_page, cobb.loads_tab, ops_notes.railcars]", 'VR App. 1'),

