    ("4.6", "Density above formation fluid threshold for safe injection", "Pass", "Density at 15°C 1.192 g/cm³ (ASTM D4052). Formation fluid: Waypoint Analytical report 24-200-0020, Lab No 98021, page 5, 'Specific Gravity 1.01 g/mL', ASTM D-1298-85 (opened this session). The bio-oil is denser than the formation fluid. [log:lab_results.density_15C_g_cm3, lab_results.formation_fluid]", "UIC Permit / safe injection"),

    ("SECTION", "5. Ops Notes Accuracy & Internal Consistency", "", "", ""),
    ('5.1', 'Correct batch ID and injection week in Ops Notes', 'Flag', "'AECN Rail'!B2 reads INJ-09-2026-W3, week 2026-09-11 to 2026-09-18; all 10 offload rows dated 2026-09-18; Certify period 2026-09-12 to 2026-09-18, inside the guidance's W3 window '11 – 18 September 2026'. Label error: A3/A4 read 'Week Start (Sat)' and 'Week End (Sat)' but 2026-09-11 and 2026-09-18 are Fridays; W2's Ops week ran Saturday 2026-09-05 to Saturday 2026-09-12, so 2026-09-11 and 2026-09-12 fall in both weeks' windows (no offload is booked twice). [log:ops_notes.batch_id_cell, ops_notes.week_start, ops_notes.week_end, ops_notes.week_labels, ops_notes.offload_table, certify.removal_period, vvb_guidance.quote_scope]", 'verify header'),
    ("5.2", "Scale ticket values correctly transcribed into Ops Notes", "Flag", "Ops D/E equal the 20 ticket gross weights exactly. Ticket labels are inconsistent: GPRX5102 offload 2's full ticket 1124426253554 carries commodity 'SHPX215046 O4' and TILX200231 offload 4's full ticket 1124426255569 carries 'SHPX215046 3', both naming another railcar; W2 booked SHPX215046 offloads 3-4 on different tickets (1124426250545 and 1124426250546). TILX200231 labels also vary ('TIMX200231 O1', 'TILX2000231 O1', 'TILX2000231 O2'). [log:scale_tickets.pair_comparison, scale_tickets.w2_shpx215046_tickets, mass_chain.counts]", "VR Sec 5.1"),
    ("5.3", "Oil and aqueous phase mass reconciliation", "N/A", "AECN-only removal, no aqueous phase. [log:oil_type]", ""),
    ("5.4", "COBB values present and match Ops Notes/Certify", "Flag", "COBB tab 'Basco Injection -- COBB' rows 1776-1785 (import 2026-09-29 11:54:56), column A 'INJ-09-2026-W3_bio_oil' confirmed before reading: all 10 offloaded_quantity_kg equal the Ops nets (mass-chain cobb_offload_consistency 10 of 10 PASS), consumed_lot follows Rail_<railcar>_<date>_offload_N and BOL_number lists each railcar's three BOLs. Two issues: an earlier import of the same 10 rows sits at rows 848-857, where row 856 has quantity_consumed_in_injection 61,207.70448 kg against offloaded 20,402.56816 kg; origin_quantity_kg for GPRX5102 is 77,950 kg against the corrected BOL total 77,940 kg (Ops M10: 'known break, not reconciled'). Neither reaches Certify. [log:cobb.tab, cobb.row_id_at_qa, cobb.batch_id_col_a, cobb.offloaded_quantity_kg, cobb.origin_quantity_kg, cobb.duplicate_block_difference, ops_notes.railcars, mass_chain.counts]", "COBB tracker"),
    ("5.5", "pH measurement noted", "Fail", "pH is blank on all 10 offload rows (G28:G37), in the rollup G46, and in COBB injection_ph on all 10 rows. pH is required for every batch; W2 had the same gap. pH is not a Certify datapoint, so Net CDR is unaffected. [log:ops_notes.ph_column_G28_G37, ops_notes.rollup.pH_avg, cobb.injection_ph_all_rows]", "GHG Stmt Sec C"),
    ("5.6", "Completion date present and matches COBB", "Pass", "COBB injection_completion_date 2026-09-18 on all 10 rows; Ops offload rows dated 2026-09-18; Certify period ends 2026-09-18. [log:cobb.injection_completion_date, ops_notes.offload_table, certify.removal_period]", "VR Sec 3.5"),
    ("5.7", "No erroneous density measurements", "N/A", "Density field expected blank for AECN in Ops Notes; the lab density is used only for the safe-injection check (4.6). [log:oil_type]", ""),

    ("SECTION", "6. AECN Feedstock Emissions & Allocation", "", "", ""),
    ("6.1", "AECN process emissions LCA CI spreadsheet present", "Pass", "'Bioenergy AE Cote-Nord Canada - LCA CI calculation - 1Jan2026 to 30Jun2026.xlsx' is in Certify Sources, linked to the pyrolysis-process CI datapoint; downloaded and opened: Summary!E19 0.13305202780074143 t CO2eq/t, period 2026-01-01 to 2026-06-30. [log:lca_files.vendor_ci, certify.attachment_map]", "VR App. 1"),
    ("6.2", "LCA with stack emissions file present", "Pass", "'FH 2026 LCA w Stack Emissions.xlsx' is linked to the same datapoint; Sheet1!I12 'Total Process Emissions MT CO2e/MT Bio Oil' 0.1371171258 (stack I10 0.004065098048 + vendor I11 0.133052027800741). [log:lca_files.fh_2026, certify.attachment_map]", "VR App. 1"),
    ("6.3", "Supporting GHG data file present", "Pass", "'Supporting GHG data 30Jun2026 S.xlsx' is linked to the same datapoint; opened: 'Inputs for LCA CI calculation for the period 1 Jan to 30 June 2026', production 10,334,884.34 L. [log:lca_files.supporting_ghg, certify.attachment_map]", "VR App. 1"),
    ("6.4", "AECN pyrolysis process EF matches current half-year value", "Pass", "Certify CI 0.13712 tCO2e/t against Standard EF sheet 2026 tab row 4 'Production Emissions for AECN Oil--H2 2026', Final Quantity 0.1371171258 (source 'FH 2026 LCA w Stack Emissions'); the removal falls in H2 2026. Certify's value is the sheet value rounded up at the fifth decimal, 0.000567 t more emission (recompute section 4). [log:standard_efs.row4_aecn_process_H2_2026, standard_efs.vs_certify.aecn_process, standard_efs.period_basis, recompute.findings]", "Certify Component Inputs"),
    ("6.5", "AECN pyrolysis embodied EF applied", "Pass", "Certify CI 0.02116 tCO2e/t; Standard EF sheet row 5 'Embodied Emissions for AECN Oil' Final Quantity 0.02116; 'AECN Embodied Emissions Calc Sheet (1).pdf' (linked, opened) gives 0.02115941123. [log:standard_efs.row5_aecn_embodied, lca_files.aecn_ee_calc, certify.attachment_map]", "Certify Datapoints"),
    ('6.6', 'Mass basis for pyrolysis EFs is pre-sparging origin mass', 'Fail', "Both pyrolysis components use 'Bio-Oil Mass - AECN via Rail' 197,321.59 kg, the sum of the 10 pre-sparging ticket nets (Ops C46), which covers the delivered oil. GPRX5102 and TILX200231 are fully drawn and lost 186.38656 kg between loading and offload; that oil was produced and was in Charm custody, so its pyrolysis emissions (0.029501 t) also belong to this removal and are not charged (8.2). [log:certify.components, ops_notes.rollup.mass_used_kg, ops_notes.railcars, policy.custody_rule, recompute.findings]", 'Certify Components'),

    ("SECTION", "7. Gross-to-Net Calculation", "", "", ""),
    ("7.1", "Gross CO2e = injectate mass x carbon wt% x 3.667", "Fail", "Certify applies the formula to its own inputs correctly (194.39438206 t x 0.397 x 3.667 gives 282.999147 t), but its mass input is 902.44 kg too high (2.7). From the Ops MOBI, 193.4919399 t x 0.397 x 3.667 gives 281.685373 t, so the sequestration is overstated by 1.313774 tCO2e. [log:certify.components, _derived_values.gross_internal_calc, recompute.findings]", "GHG Stmt Sec E"),
    ('7.2', 'Process emissions correctly deducted', 'Fail', 'Activities 46.439 t in the Calculation view equal pyrolysis 31.232061 t (27.056736 + 4.175325) plus bio-oil transport 15.206929 t (process 14.634650 + embodied 0.572279), and every component recomputes (9.2, 9.4). The total leaves out 0.042411 t of upstream emissions on the 186.38656 kg lost from GPRX5102 and TILX200231 (8.2); with it charged, activities are 46.481401 t. [log:certify.calc_view, certify.components, _derived_values.activities_calc, recompute.findings]', 'GHG Stmt Sec E'),
    ('7.3', 'Uncertainty discount correctly applied', 'Pass', "Calculation view: 'Net 249.637 = Sequestrations 282.999 + Adjustments 14.635 - Activities 46.439 - Uncertainty Discount 1.558'. Re-derived from the component inputs: sequestration one-sigma (mass +/- 725.7 kg on 194,394.38206 kg, carbon +/- 0.15883 on 39.7 %) combined with the mass-driven activities' one-sigma (+/- 725.7 kg on 197,321.59 kg) reproduces 1.5577199676 t (recompute section 8), 0.55 % of gross. [log:certify.calc_view, certify.uncertainty_discount_t, recompute.lines, _derived_values.discount_pct_calc]", 'Isometric Standard v2.0 S3.7'),
    ("7.4", "Net removals consistent with BCU Quant and GHG Statement", "Flag", "Certify's GHG statements list (read today) ends at '01 Aug 2026 to 31 Aug 2026', Certificates issued 10 Sep 2026; the September 2026 statement has not been created, so there is no RP-level BCU Quant or GHG statement to cross-check yet. [log:rp_status]", "RP BCU Quant.xlsx"),

    ("SECTION", "7a. Per-Component Uncertainty Verification", "", "", ""),
    ("7a.1", "Layer 1 - every component that needs uncertainty has it on the right input", "Pass", "All 10 component detail views opened. Injection sequestration shows +/- on carbon and mass; both pyrolysis components and the three transport-process legs show +/- on their mass input; the three transport-embodied components are per-mile with no mass input; the BCU is a constant reduction. None carries +/- on a distance or factor input. [log:certify.modal_reads, certify.components]", "MRV Uncertainty Cheat Sheet"),
    ("7a.2", "Layer 2 - reported +/- matches the expected value", "Pass", "Mass +/- 725.7 kg on every mass input: 10 offload weighings x 72.57 kg, one outbound weighing per offload (Failure Category 9). Carbon +/- 0.15883 % against 0.004 x 39.7 = 0.1588 %. [log:certify.modal_reads, certify.components, _derived_values.unc_calc]", "Isometric Standard S3.7.3"),
    ('7a.3', 'Layer 3 - discount present and consistent', 'Pass', 'Uncertainty Discount 1.5577199676 t is present in the Calculation view, carried into the net, and reproduces from the per-component inputs (7.3; recompute section 8). The cross-check against the GHG statement waits for the September statement (7.4). [log:certify.uncertainty_discount_t, certify.calc_view, recompute.lines, rp_status]', 'Isometric Standard S3.7.3'),

    ("SECTION", "8. Data Integrity & Anomaly Check", "", "", ""),
    ('8.1', 'No unexplained outliers in mass, carbon or calculated values', 'Flag', "Nets run 39,740 to 46,420 lb, full gross 68,080 to 75,300 lb, and carbon sits 0.046 SD from the mean. Three tickets split their axles unlike the rest: full tickets GPRX5102 offload 2 (1124426253554: steer 0, drive 25,680, trailer 45,580, gross 71,260 lb) and TILX200231 offload 2 (1124426254565: steer 0, drive 22,160, trailer 50,480, gross 72,640 lb), where every other full ticket reads 9,820 to 13,060 lb on the steer; and empty ticket TILX200231 offload 1 (1312226254521: steer 3,880, drive 16,900 lb), where the other empties read 9,420 to 10,640 lb on the steer. Each gross is the sum of its readings and sits in range, and every ticket states 'The GROSS WEIGHT is the CERTIFIED WEIGHT and was weighed on a full length platform scale', so the nets stand. [log:scale_tickets.offloads.GPRX5102_offload_2, scale_tickets.offloads.TILX200231_offload_2, scale_tickets.axle_notes, _derived_values.ticket_ranges_calc, _derived_values.carbon_z_calc]", 'GHG Stmt Sec C'),
    ('8.2', 'Spills, losses and irregularities documented', 'Fail', "GPRX5102 offloaded 121.75648 kg (0.156 %) less than loaded and TILX200231 64.63008 kg (0.083 %), recorded in Ops G10 and G12; the September guidance discloses no spill. Upstream emissions of all oil in Charm custody are netted against removals, but pyrolysis, AECN-SOPOR truck and rail emissions are charged on the offloaded 197,321.59 kg, so the lost 186.38656 kg carries none of them: pyrolysis 0.029501 t + truck 0.002290 t + rail 0.010620 t, 0.042411 t uncharged (Certify factors). The August guidance applied the same principle to the GPRX5139 spill: 'The full 77,800 kg carries its upstream burden — pyrolysis, truck to SOPOR, rail, and truck to Basco — while only the 74,380.92 kg that reached the wellhead earns a removal.' [log:ops_notes.railcars, vvb_guidance.august_spill_quote, vvb_guidance.no_other_sections, policy.custody_rule, recompute.findings, _derived_values.loss_upstream_calc]", 'GHG Stmt Sec C'),
    ('8.3', 'Inventory reconciliation / carryover documented', 'Fail', "SHPX215046 is drawn across two weeks and out of order: offloads 1-2 weighed 2026-09-06/07 are booked here, offloads 3-4 weighed 2026-09-07/08 were booked in W2. The guidance reads 'Where a railcar is offloaded across more than one reporting week, the loaded mass is recorded once, in the week the railcar’s first offload occurs, and subsequent weeks draw against the same shipment.' W3 records the 77,680 kg loaded mass again with H11 'Previously Claimed' 0 against the 35,652.3312 kg W2 booked, so the attached Ops Notes shows the railcar PARTIAL (F11 42,047.9784 kg, G11 blank) although all four offloads are booked; with H11 at 35,652.3312 kg, F11 reads 77,700.3096 kg and the 20.3096 kg over-draw (2.5) shows. The attached record misstates the railcar balance a verifier would check; H11 should carry W2's draw, 35,652.3312 kg as booked today and 35,632.0216 kg once W2's offload 4 is cut back. [log:policy.last_load_ruling, ops_notes.railcars, mass_chain.shpx215046_balance, w2_live_ops, vvb_guidance.quote_multi_week]", 'VR Sec 3.5'),
    ("8.4", "Rail uncertainty conservatism: offloads at least equal inbound BOLs", "Pass", "GPRX5102 and TILX200231: 4 offloads each against 3 inbound BOLs; SHPX215046: 4 offloads (2 in W2, 2 here) against 3 BOLs. Per-offload uncertainty (7a.2) books more than the inbound weighings would. [log:mass_chain.rail_uncertainty_precondition, bols.per_railcar]", "Isometric Standard S3.7.3"),

    ("SECTION", "9. Isometric Certify - Removal Component Mapping", "", "", ""),
    ("9.1", "SEQUESTRATIONS: gross injection sequestration matches internal gross", "Fail", "Injection sequestration 282.999147 tCO2e reproduces from Certify's inputs (7.1) but not from the evidence: the Ops MOBI gives 281.685373 tCO2e, 1.313774 t lower, because Certify's Mass of Injectant omits the 902.44 kg R&D removal (2.7). [log:certify.components, _derived_values.gross_internal_calc, recompute.findings]", "Certify Components"),
    ('9.2', 'ACTIVITIES - Transport: process + embodied correct for all legs', 'Fail', "All six legs recomputed from the Standard EF sheet 2026 tab (tanker 0.0001143 MT/(t·mi) and 0.0002375605888 MT/mi; rail 2.5910374e-05 MT/(t·mi) and 3.113066508e-05 MT/mi): process 2.424477, 11.242775 (Certify 11.242613) and 0.967560 t; embodied 0.194514 (Certify 0.194488), 0.173968 (Certify 0.173964) and 0.203827 t. Certify carries the rail fuel factor as 0.02591 kg/(t·mi), the sheet's 0.025910374 rounded, so its rail process is 0.000162 t lower; every difference is under 0.001 t. Transport process 14.634650 t plus embodied 0.572279 t gives the Bio-oil transport subtotal 15.206929 t. The railcar embodied value is the 2026 figure (65.37 MTCO2e / 2,100,000 mi). The upstream process legs are charged on the offloaded 197,321.59 kg, so the 186.38656 kg lost in GPRX5102 and TILX200231 carries no AECN-SOPOR truck (0.002290 t) or rail (0.010620 t) emissions (8.2). [log:policy.custody_rule, standard_efs, recompute.findings, recompute.lines, route_evidence.railcar_ee_pdf, _derived_values.transport_calc, _derived_values.activities_calc]", 'Certify Components'),
    ("9.3", "ACTIVITIES - Injection: LCS / sample transport", "N/A", "AECN needs no LCS pre-treatment; none of the 10 components is an injection-side activity. [log:certify.components]", "Certify Components"),
    ("9.4", "ACTIVITIES - Pyrolysis: process + embodied entries present", "Pass", "'AECN pyrolysis (from rail loads) - process emissions' 27.056736 t (197.32159 t x 0.13712) and '... - embodied emissions' 4.175325 t (197.32159 t x 0.02116), both recomputed. [log:certify.components, recompute.lines]", "Certify Components"),
    ("9.5", "REDUCTIONS: applicable BCU categories populated", "Pass", "'BCU - Transport Process', Constant CO₂ reduction 14,635 kgCO2e, sourced to Charm-RetirementCertificate-RD-EACs-20251218.pdf (opened: 2,795 Renewable Diesel TERCs retired Dec 18 2025, vintage 2024; 'Each TERC represents one metric ton of carbon dioxide equivalent (\"tCO2e\") reduced.'). Transportation Emissions Accounting v1.1 §4.0: 'the use of Book and Claim Units (BCUs) for low-carbon fuels to substitute for some, or all, of project fuel usage is permitted'. Only the transport-process category applies to this removal. [log:bcu_sources]", "Certify Components"),
    ('9.6', 'REDUCTIONS - BCU does not exceed transport process emissions', 'Fail', "BCU 14.635 t against a transport-process sum of 14.634650 t (AECN-SOPOR 2.424477 t, rail 11.242613 t and Opelousas-Basco 0.967560 t, Certify values; 14.634812 t with sheet factors): the BCU exceeds the emission it offsets by 0.35 kg (0.19 kg at sheet precision). §4.2.1 Eq 5 allows at most the BCUs for which '(F_j − F_BCU,j ED_BCU,j/ED_Fuel,Transportation,j) ≥ 0'. The fix is the exact process figure, not a rounded one: 14,634.650 kgCO2e on today's activities, 14,647.560 kgCO2e once the lost oil's truck and rail emissions are charged (8.2), 14,647.392 kgCO2e with the 2.3 standard empty weight as well. [log:bcu_sources, policy.bcu_fix_rule, recompute.findings, _derived_values.bcu_calc]", 'Certify Components / Calculation View'),
    ("9.7", "COUNTERFACTUALS: zero per protocol", "Pass", "The Calculation view carries no counterfactual term: Sequestrations, Adjustments, Activities and Uncertainty Discount only (7.3). [log:certify.calc_view]", "Certify Components"),
    ('9.8', 'Net removal matches internal calculation', 'Fail', "249.637 t reproduces from Certify's own terms (recompute 249.637427). It does not reproduce from the evidence: with the R&D removal deducted (2.7), gross 281.685373 t, BCU at the process sum 14.634650 t, activities 46.438990 t and the discount re-derived on the corrected mass 1.553904 t give 248.327129 t, 1.309871 t below Certify. Charging the lost oil's upstream emissions (8.2) gives 248.297628 t, and the 2.3 standard empty weight as well gives 248.294746 t (recompute CORRECTIONS). [log:certify.calc_view, recompute.findings, recompute.lines, _derived_values.net_internal_calc]", 'Certify Calculation View'),
    ("9.9", "All datapoints have descriptive source names", "Flag", "'image (44).png' is a generic filename on the rail distance datapoint; the image is a Watco email screenshot naming no railcar, route or date. 'Standard Emission Factors + Calculations (8).xlsx' is uploaded twice (two source records, byte-identical). The Standard EF sheet cites 'GLEC V3.2 2025' for the tanker and rail factors while the attached framework is the 'v3.1 edition, revised and updated (2024)'; its rail value 16.1 g CO2e/t-km converts to the sheet's 2.5910374e-05 MT/(t·mi), so only the version label differs. [log:route_evidence.watco_email, certify.certify_sources_enumeration_note, standard_efs.glec_version_cited, route_evidence.glec]", "Certify Datapoints"),
    ("9.10", "All Sources match files in the batch folder / Ops Notes links", "Pass", "43 source records (42 filenames) enumerated with their linked datapoints. Every file that also exists in Drive was downloaded from Certify and matched byte-for-byte: 20 scale tickets, 9 BOLs and the SGS certificate; the Certify Ops Notes matches the live sheet on the AECN Rail and AECN Truck tabs (its Summary differs only by later Kerry rows). The route images, LCA files, EF extracts, BCU certificate and GLEC framework are Certify-only and were opened there. [log:certify.certify_sources_enumeration, certify.ticket_sources_compare, certify.bol_sources_compare, certify.sources_downloaded_and_opened]", "Certify Sources"),

